Module fixture.values.

Define Tier as one of Gold, Silver.

Define Point has x, label, ratio.

Rule intValue given x, produce:
  Return x plus 1.

Rule longValue given x, produce:
  Return x times 3000000000000000L.

Rule doubleValue given x, produce:
  Return x divided by 7.

Rule halfValue given x, produce:
  Return x divided by 2.

Rule decimalValue given x, produce:
  Return 1.10m plus 2.205m.

Rule textValue given x, produce:
  Return "Grüße, 世界".

Rule boolValue given x, produce:
  Return x greater than 3.

Rule double given x, produce:
  Return x times 2.

Rule listValue given xs, produce:
  Return List.map(xs, double).

Rule mapValue given a, b, produce:
  Return Map.put(Map.put(Map.empty(), a, 1), b, 2).

Rule dataValue given x, produce:
  Return Point with x set to x and label set to "p" and ratio set to x divided by 4.

Rule enumValue given x, produce:
  If x greater than 700:
    Return Gold.
  Return Silver.

Rule someValue given x, produce:
  Return Some(x).

Rule noneValue given x, produce:
  Return None.

Rule okValue given x, produce:
  Return Ok(x).

Rule errValue given x, produce:
  Return Err("bad").

Rule verdictAllow given x, produce Verdict:
  Return Verdict.allow().

Rule verdictDeny given x, produce Verdict:
  Return Verdict.deny("over limit").

Rule verdictApproval given x, produce Verdict:
  Return Verdict.require_approval("Credit Officer", "large exposure").

Rule decimalTrailing given x, produce:
  Return x times 1.0825m.

Rule decimalZero given x, produce:
  Return 0.00m.

Rule decimalNegative given x, produce:
  Return 0m minus 1.50m.

Rule decimalSmall given x, produce:
  Return 0.000001m.
